ksh93: an unknown character class is an error, not a jump.

regclass looks a [:class:] name up in its table, then, where the C
library has wctype, asks wctype. Amix has no wctype: an unknown name
left the search one entry past the end of the table, and regclass
returned whatever lay there as the class's function. A pattern such as
[[:bogus:]] made ksh jump to a data address. Without wctype an unknown
name is now no class.

--- a/programs/dtksh/ksh93/src/lib/libast/regex/regclass.c
+++ b/programs/dtksh/ksh93/src/lib/libast/regex/regclass.c
@@ -212,7 +212,10 @@
 		if (n == cp->size && strneq(s, cp->name, n) && (!cp->next || cp->next == lc))
 			goto found;
 	}
-#if _lib_wctype
+#if !_lib_wctype
+	/* not a class: cp is past the end of the table */
+	return 0;
+#else
 	if (!(cp = zp))
 	{
 		if (!(cp = xp))
